  "schema_version": "2.0",
  "description": "Curated concepts. family defaults to the clinical type's concept family; only records of that family join the concept. A record joins a concept when its source code is listed under match.codes, or its normalized name is listed under match.names or matches match.name_patterns, or its structured symptom or exposure key matches match.key_patterns (optionally limited to match.categories). Codings marked curated_standard_code are mappings made here, never codes the source supplied; they are not copied into records. Records with an unlisted source code join a concept for that code; symptom and exposure records join a concept for their structured key; others join a concept for their normalized name. A medication concept may state its generic name (lowercase, the shared identity used for pooling) and brands (lowercase names its records may use, each pooled as a separate connection when a record names it). Without a curated generic, a clinical list's generic (BRAND) convention supplies both.",
